  "preamble": "Labiodentalization of the voiced bilabial fricative [β] to [v] moves the constriction from both lips to the lower lip against the upper teeth. Greek is the textbook case: the Koine fricative [β] that had replaced Attic [b] became Medieval and Modern Greek [v], so βάρος went /bá.ros/ > /ˈβa.ros/ > /ˈva.ros/. Proto-Germanic medial [β] likewise became [v] in Old English and Old Norse (*gebaną > giefan, gefa). In Welsh and Cornish the Proto-Brythonic lenited *β became /v/ (*aβon > afon, avon).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Labiodentalization",
